# Build the articulated `{{ object_name }}`: bpy links + hand-written URDF

You write TWO files: `src/model.py` (raw bpy — one mesh object per LINK, authored in WORLD
coordinates at the rest pose) and `src/robot.urdf` (native URDF describing the joints). The harness
exports each link to `meshes/<link>.glb`, lints the URDF, runs forward kinematics, sweeps every joint
between its limits and checks for penetrations, then renders rest + limit poses for a judge.

