## Acceptance checklist
{{ acceptance }}

## DO
- Build every link at its WORLD rest pose with the plan's bbox centre/extents (±0.01 m); each link is
  ONE object (join sub-shapes into it) named exactly as the link.
- Joint origins: every link frame sits at its joint's world pivot (root at the world origin), so the
  URDF `<joint><origin xyz>` = pivot_child − pivot_parent (plain subtraction of world points; root
  parent pivot = 0 0 0). The harness exports meshes/<link>.glb in WORLD coordinates, therefore the
  child's visual AND collision `<origin xyz>` = −P (the NEGATED world pivot; root link: `0 0 0`) —
  never the mesh-centre offset. Keep the numbers consistent with the bbox centres in the table —
  write them out explicitly as comments in the URDF before the joint.
- Use the axis vectors from the table verbatim; limits = lower/upper from the table; `effort`/
  `velocity` any positive numbers.
- Keep ≥ 0.003 m clearance along each joint's motion direction between the child link and the
  links it moves past (drawer vs cabinet walls, door vs frame); fixed neighbours overlap ≥ 0.002 m.
- Hinged lids/doors pivot at their EDGE (the hinge line), drawers slide along the cabinet depth.

## DON'T
- No camera/light/render/export calls in bpy; no imports beyond bpy/bmesh/math/mathutils/random.
- No links that float (every non-root link touches its parent at rest, or is attached by its joint
  at a pivot that lies ON the child link's geometry ± 0.01 m).
- No joint whose child passes through another link anywhere in [lower, upper].
- No renaming of links/joints; no extra root links; one tree rooted at `{{ root_link }}` as planned.

